  weekTwoToast:"Eight in the morning. Doña Chelo is unlocking the gate on the southwest lot — and leaving it open. Nothing behind you closes either.",
  mepi1:"Saturday, closing time. Doña Chelo counts the drawer twice, the way she has for thirty years, and this time the number matches what the screen said all week. “You didn't build me a robot,” she says. “You built me a Tuesday I can trust.” Frijol sleeps on the scale. Outside, somebody is laying track. Before you're out the door she's on the landline. “Tacho. He told me to stop paying him for something. Send him your worst.”",
  mepi2:"Saturday, closing time. Some of it stuck, some of it Nando quietly went back to doing by hand. Doña Chelo shrugs. “Half of it works. That's more than the last guy.” She writes your name on the wall by the register, next to the permit — and under a name in older handwriting you don't recognize yet. On the landline, later: “Tacho. Half of what he did works. That's more than the last one.”",
  mepi3:"Saturday, closing time. The mercado survived you. Most of the list is still a list, and the pilot is a folder nobody opens — but Doña Chelo hands you a bag of pan dulce anyway. “Come back when you've thought about it.” The door does not lock behind you. A week later she phones Tacho and says one thing: “He's honest about what he doesn't know. Start there.”",
